# Meeting Scheduling (Python, Timefold, FastAPI)

## Problem Description

Schedule meetings between employees, where:
* Each meeting has a topic, duration, required and preferred attendees.
* Each meeting needs a room with sufficient capacity.
* Meetings should not overlap with other meetings if they share resources (room or attendees).
* Meetings should be scheduled as soon as possible.
* Preferred attendees should be able to attend if possible.

## Problem Size

* 24 meetings
* 20 people
* 3 rooms
* 4 days of time grains (15-minute intervals)

## Running the Application

```shell
cd python/meeting-scheduling
python -m uvicorn meeting_scheduling.rest_api:app --reload
```

Then open http://localhost:8000 in your web browser.

## REST API

The application exposes a REST API with the following endpoints:

* `GET /demo-data`: List all available demo data sets
* `GET /demo-data/{dataset_id}`: Get a specific demo data set
* `GET /schedules`: List all job IDs of submitted schedules
* `GET /schedules/{problem_id}`: Get the solution and score for a given job ID
* `GET /schedules/{problem_id}/status`: Get the schedule status and score for a given job ID
* `DELETE /schedules/{problem_id}`: Terminate solving for a given job ID
* `POST /schedules`: Submit a schedule to start solving
* `PUT /schedules/analyze`: Submit a schedule to analyze its score

## Solution Strategy

The solver uses a constraint provider to define the constraints:

* Hard constraints:
  * Room conflict: A room can accommodate at most one meeting at the same time
  * Avoid overtime: Don't schedule meetings outside of working hours
  * Required attendance conflict: A person cannot attend two meetings at the same time
  * Required room capacity: A room must have sufficient capacity for all attendees
  * Start and end on same day: A meeting must start and end on the same day

* Medium constraints:
  * Required and preferred attendance conflict: Avoid scheduling meetings with required and preferred attendees at the same time
  * Preferred attendance conflict: Avoid scheduling meetings with preferred attendees at the same time

* Soft constraints:
  * Do meetings as soon as possible: Schedule meetings earlier rather than later
  * One break between consecutive meetings: Allow a break between meetings
  * Overlapping meetings: Minimize the number of overlapping meetings
  * Assign larger rooms first: Prefer larger rooms for earlier meetings
  * Room stability: Prefer to keep meetings in the same room
